The site's second change to the scene of "White Room, Pixel Traced": a Monstera
deliciosa in a terracotta pot, applied by scripts/vendor-whiteroom.sh after
scripts/whiteroom-scene.patch.

The plant is the scene's 8th group (the renderer takes up to 8), at the left of
the room, where the site's wide frames show it and the page's 3:2 frame does not.
Its primitives come from ../monstera-scene.js, the site's own code: new kinds
(LEAF, CONE, CLUSTER) and materials (LEAF .. SOIL), which whiteroom.ts teaches
the room's shader (monstera-shader.ts). The leaves' maturities go out with the
scene, for the leaf maps the renderer bakes. The uplighter's cable is rerouted
over its last metre so that its end disappears behind the pot's saucer instead
of stopping on the open floor.

